config BR2_PACKAGE_IPPUSB
	bool "ippusb (driverless USB printing)"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_CUPS
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_LIBUSB
	help
	  Driverless printing for USB printers, for printers that have no
	  classic driver.

	  Printers made since roughly 2016 advertise IPP Everywhere /
	  AirPrint and rasterise pages themselves, so the host sends them a
	  PDF and no per-model driver is involved. Manufacturers stopped
	  shipping drivers for them, so the Gutenprint / brlaser / splix
	  driver library does not cover them, and handing one a driver it
	  cannot parse makes it accept the job and print nothing.

	  The usual answer, the ipp-usb daemon, proxies a localhost TCP port
	  onto the printer. That is impossible on this kernel, which has no
	  IP stack at all. But the IPP-USB protocol is HTTP carried on USB
	  bulk endpoints, so this backend speaks it directly over libusb and
	  builds the queue's PPD from the printer's own reported attributes.

comment "ippusb needs CUPS and libusb"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_CUPS || !BR2_PACKAGE_LIBUSB
